PhysioExperiment adapter for OmicsLake
}
\details{
An \link[OmicsLake:LakeAdapter]{OmicsLake::LakeAdapter} that stores and retrieves \link[PhysioCore:PhysioExperiment]{PhysioCore::PhysioExperiment}
objects in an OmicsLake with full fidelity.

A \code{PhysioExperiment} is a \code{SummarizedExperiment} subclass with one extra slot
(\code{samplingRate}); its provenance, events, and derived estimates live in
\code{metadata()}. OmicsLake's generic \code{SEAdapter} already round-trips assays,
\code{colData}, \code{rowData}, and \code{metadata}, but it reconstructs a \emph{plain}
\code{SummarizedExperiment} -- losing the class identity and the sampling rate.
This adapter inherits \code{SEAdapter} and adds only that missing piece: it stashes
the sampling rate in metadata on \code{put()} and rebuilds a \code{PhysioExperiment} on
\code{get()}. Because provenance is carried in \code{metadata()}, it survives the round
trip unchanged (verified: \code{provenanceHash()} is identical before and after),
so the ecosystem's per-object (micro) W3C-PROV provenance lands intact next to
OmicsLake's cross-dataset (macro) lineage. Assays that are not 2-D matrices
(e.g. epoched \emph{time x channel x trial} arrays), which the generic \code{SEAdapter}
would collapse when storing them as flat tables, are likewise stashed in
metadata and spliced back in their original order on \code{get()}.

A higher \code{priority()} than the generic \code{SEAdapter} ensures this adapter is
selected for \code{PhysioExperiment} objects (which also satisfy \code{SEAdapter}).
}
